## 3. Tech stack (decided — swap only if BOTH sides agree)

### 3.1 Choices

| Part | Choice |
|---|---|
| **Frontend** | **React 18 + TypeScript + Vite** · React Router v6 · TanStack Query v5 · Zustand (auth/session only) · Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui · Recharts · react-hook-form + zod · lucide-react · sonner (toasts) · date-fns · **MSW** (mock API) · native `WebSocket` |
| **Backend** | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI** · Uvicorn · SQLAlchemy 2.0 (async) + asyncpg · Alembic · Pydantic v2 + pydantic-settings · PyJWT · argon2-cffi · cryptography (Fernet) · APScheduler 3.x · httpx · numpy · pytest |
| **Database** | **PostgreSQL 16** (no MongoDB — the data is relational and the solution diagram specifies PostgreSQL) |
| **Cloud SDKs** | `boto3` (AWS), `azure-identity` + `azure-mgmt-*` (Azure), `google-cloud-*` (GCP). **Optional extras**, imported lazily inside live adapters so mock mode needs none of them |
| **LLM** | Any provider behind an `LlmClient` interface (default: Anthropic Claude via the `anthropic` SDK). Model + key from env |
| **Realtime** | FastAPI native WebSocket at `/ws` |
| **Deploy** | Docker Compose: `db` + `backend` + `frontend` (nginx serves the React build **and** reverse-proxies `/api` and `/ws` → single origin, no CORS pain) |

### 3.2 Why FastAPI (not MERN)
- Python has the best cloud SDK coverage (boto3 etc.) and the numeric tools (numpy) needed for anomaly detection, trends and forecasting.
- MERN implies MongoDB; our diagram and data model are PostgreSQL.
- FastAPI auto-generates OpenAPI docs (`/api/docs`) from the same Pydantic models the code uses → easy contract checking between separately built parts.
- Native WebSockets, async I/O for slow cloud calls, one small Docker image to deploy.
- *(If the team is far stronger in JS, Node + Express + Prisma + PostgreSQL could implement the same contract — but this file assumes FastAPI.)*

