## 9. WebSocket contract

**URL:** `/ws?token=<accessToken>` (browser builds `ws(s)://<host>/ws` unless `VITE_WS_URL` is set).
**Auth failure / expired token:** server closes with code **4401** → client refreshes the token (§7.1) and reconnects. The client also reconnects whenever the access token is refreshed.

**Client → server**
```json
{ "action": "subscribe",   "channels": ["dashboard", "alerts", "actions", "recommendations", "resource:b4a2e0d1-0c3e-4f6a-8d75-2f7c9a1e5b30"] }
{ "action": "unsubscribe", "channels": ["resource:b4a2e0d1-0c3e-4f6a-8d75-2f7c9a1e5b30"] }
{ "action": "ping" }
```

**Server → client (always this envelope)**
```json
{ "event": "metric.updated", "channel": "resource:b4a2e0d1-...", "ts": "2026-09-19T10:31:05Z", "data": { } }
```

| `event` | Channel | `data` |
|---|---|---|
| `metric.updated` | `resource:{id}` / `dashboard` | `{ resourceId, metric, unit, point: { t, v } }` |
| `resource.health_changed` | `dashboard` | `{ resourceId, from: Health, to: Health }` |
| `anomaly.detected` | `alerts` | `Anomaly` |
| `alert.created` / `alert.resolved` | `alerts` | `Alert` |
| `recommendation.created` | `recommendations` | `Recommendation` |
| `action.status_changed` | `actions` | `{ actionId, status: ActionStatus, message: string }` |
| `cost.updated` | `dashboard` | `{ monthToDateUsd, forecastEndOfMonthUsd }` |
| `notification.created` | *(automatic, per user)* | `Notification` |
| `pong` | – | `{}` |

**Rules:** server pushes metric events at most every 5 s per resource · client pings every 25 s · client auto-reconnects with backoff (1 s → 30 s) · if WS is down the frontend **falls back to polling every 15 s** · WS is read-only for the UI (all writes go through REST) · `recommendation.created` payload is computed for the receiving user's role (`policyCheck`).

